wn for."]],"soil":{"rock":"Sand is warm and airy. It drains fast but holds little water, and phylloxera does not thrive in it. Clay holds water well but drains poorly. It stays cool, which slows ripening and keeps acidity up.","top":"The topsoil drains well and still stores water for dry spells, so vines grow evenly. Its pH is close to neutral, so vines take up the nutrients they need easily."},"land":[["Slope","Mostly flat. Easy and cheap to farm by machine, but on still nights cold air settles on flat ground, so spring frost is a bigger risk."]]},"winkler":["Ib","Early-ripening grapes reach high quality."],"wset":true,"sources":[{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Wikipedia, Winkler index (what each region suits)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Winkler_index&oldid=1379995815"},{"name":"Jones 2010, Climate, grapes, and wine: structure and suitability in a variable and changing climate, VIII International Terroir Congress (which grapes suit which growing season temperatures)","url":"https://ives-openscience.eu/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Climate_Grape_Wine_Jones.pdf"},{"name":"ISRIC SoilGrids 2.0, 1 km aggregates, 30 to 60 cm depth (CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://www.isric.org/explore/soilgrids"},{"name":"USDA NRCS Soil Survey Manual, Agriculture Handbook 18 (texture classes and pH classes)",